<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Equal or equivalent sets</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(A = {@As@}\) and \(B = {@Bs@}\).</p><p>(a) Which is true?</p><p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) Write a set \(C\) of whole numbers less than \(30\) that is equivalent to \(A\) but not equal to \(A\).</p><p>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) \(A = {@Al@}\) has \({@nA@}\) elements and \(B = {@Bl@}\) has \({@nB@}\). [[if test="is(ky=1)"]]They have exactly the same elements, so they are equal (and so also equivalent).[[elif test="is(ky=2)"]]They have the same number of elements but different elements, so they are equivalent but not equal.[[else]]They have different numbers of elements, so they are not equivalent (and so not equal).[[/if]]</p><p>(b) \(C\) needs \({@nA@}\) elements, like \(A\), but must differ from \(A\) in at least one element. For example \(C = {@dset(Cs)@}\). Many other answers are correct.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
