  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Sets: equal and equivalent sets</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core and Essential 1.1 (a): Decide whether two sets are equal, equivalent or neither, and construct a set equivalent but not equal to a given set.</p><p id="edition">Core and Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 2 (Sets), Exercise A, question 3 of School Mathematics Project, SMP Book 1 (Metric), Cambridge University Press, 1969: deciding whether two sets are equal; every pair is new, and equivalent sets and the construct part are added.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core and Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
